    "description": {
      "value": "<p><em>“Some blows land as warnings, not endings.”</em></p><ul><li>Weapons you personally forge, maintain, or sanctify can always deal <strong>non-lethal</strong> damage at your direction, even if they would not normally be able to (GM’s call for edge cases like disintegration beams).</li><li>When you lead or anchor a conflict that ends in a <strong>no-fatality victory</strong> (surrender, rout, incapacitation, or social resolution) where your work clearly mattered, your faction gains <strong>+1 Diplomacy OP</strong> for the next strategic turn (once per scenario).</li></ul><p><em>This doesn’t mean you never hurt anyone. It means you always left a door.</em></p>",
